<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
OpenH1.app's entitlements under the hardened runtime (tools/macos_app.py signs
the app with them; port/macos/README.md, "The app"):

- allow-jit: the game is a guest image whose code the host loads at start
  and makes executable (port/android/host/host_loader.c): in MAP_JIT memory,
  the narrowest way the hardened runtime allows. Without it the process is
  killed when it runs the code; allow-unsigned-executable-memory would also
  work, for any memory.
- audio-input: the microphone, for voice chat in network games (the
  hardened runtime refuses it otherwise; Info.plist's
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription is what macOS asks the player with).

Signed ad hoc (the local build), the app also gets disable-library-validation,
so that it loads its ad hoc signed SDL; a Developer ID signature does not
need it (tools/macos_app.py, sign_app).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
